"A Vestige, a condensation of the Sea from the Ninth Depth, sits in Nala's reservoir."
"The Vestige is why her reservoir has no floor and why her Scope is not fixed."
"The Vestige broke the Horizon this winter in the drowned shrine under Hollow Tarn."
"A Vestige breaks any Talented body of Teyr it enters, as it broke a young healer's in the Vale."
"The Vestige reached into the dreams at the Sea's edge for a soul no faith of Teyr had marked."
"Alan, dozing over a book, was dreaming at the Sea's edge when the Vestige reached, and it took him."
"The Sea built a body around Alan's soul and the Vestige, whole, with every tributary carved."
"The Sea remembers the drowned, and it built the body in the likeness of the last one the tarn took."
"Nala is new flesh wearing Liss Aske's face; nothing of Liss's soul or memory is in her."
"Liss Aske walked into Hollow Tarn on Threllsnacht eve, after taking off her cold iron."
"The Sea sent the Vestige as the calm against a storm rising under the Whitecombs."
"Something deep under the Whitecombs is pressing on the Horizon, and Hollow Tarn is its door."
"Undertow at its height can draw the Sea back through a tidepool and close it."
"Nala cannot go back to Earth; no road from Teyr leads there."
